Content:
	TW-JUDICIAL-PUA-XP: PUA assignments from the Big5 jfontXP.exe package
	TW-JUDICIAL-PUA-UNICODE: PUA assignments from the Unicode jfontEUDC.exe package

Regenerate both codecs:
	make gen

Regenerate either codec separately:
	make gen_judical_pua_xp
	make gen_judical_pua_unicode

The generators download the respective official package from
https://jfont.judicial.gov.tw/jfont/setup_font.html, extract 造字對照表.pdf
with bsdtar, and read it with pdftotext -layout. Each existing mapping file
is replaced only after its generation succeeds. The two packages assign
different characters to some of the same PUA code points; choose the codec
matching the font used by the input document.

Requirements: wget, bsdtar (libarchive), pdftotext (Poppler), Python 3,
and the Python bsdconv binding with bsdconv-cns11643 codecs installed.
Both codecs are included in `make` and `make install`.

The XP generator converts the PDF's CNS codes to Unicode where an installed
mapping is available, and retains CNS data otherwise. XP rows with an empty
CNS column are skipped.

The Unicode generator uses a valid non-PUA value from the source Unicode
column as a Unicode target (01). If that value is absent, private-use, or
invalid, it uses the source CNS column as a CNS11643 target (02). Rows with
no source mapping are skipped; the main CNS column contains judicial font
assignments and is not used as a fallback. Unicode output for retained CNS
data requires the corresponding CNS mappings in the installed codecs.
